From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:40:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Add an opt-in skinny BF16 GEMM for small-batch decode
 projections

sglang/srt/layers/backbone_gemm.py: a Triton kernel for y = a @ W^T with M up
to about 128 (N- and M-tiled; optional split-K whose last split sums the
per-split FP32 slots in split order, so results do not depend on scheduling;
optional programmatic dependent launch). Optional prologues form the A operand
from a Gemma add-RMSNorm or a SiLU-mul instead of reading it, in the stock
kernels' arithmetic, and a probe kernel stores that operand for tests. The
routing policy (SGLANG_BACKBONE_* switches, an (N, K, M) table, maybe_linear,
DeferredNormInput) is defined here; nothing calls it until the next patch.
